    description: "Amend docs/adr/0039-confidence-separation.md in place (per docs/adr/README.md lifecycle) with two OWNER DECISIONS taken 2026-10-15 (recorded on WI-famiv-gumof), and update docs/hypergumbo-spec.md §12 to match. Docs only; the code follows in the sibling items.\n\nRULING 6 (resolver quality interpolates within the pathway band). For an is_resolved-conditioned analyzer pathway (ast_call, ast_call_direct, macro_expansion; see evidence_types.py), a resolved edge gets\n    conf = base_unresolved + (base - base_unresolved) x resolver_score\nwhere resolver_score is the NameResolver LookupResult.confidence (1.0 exact, 0.90 path hint, 0.85 suffix, 0.70/sqrt(n) ambiguous; symbol_resolution.py ~line 202). Exact match -> the pathway base; ambiguity moves toward the unresolved base; always in band; registry-derived; preserves today's ordering. Producers pass only the resolver score. State why plain base x score was rejected: 0.85 x 0.70/sqrt(4) = 0.30, below the band floor. Say which non-call pathways (if any) also take a resolver score, or that none do.\n\nRULING 7 (linker edges are judged by the §12 linker range). Spec §12 already says linker confidence is match quality, 0.40-0.95, a separate category from analyzer edges. The analyzer band of a declared evidence_type does NOT apply to a linker edge. Record that this supersedes INV-zatu's July agent ruling that moved the websocket linker onto the analyzer band.\n\nAlso reconcile §12's sentence \"dynamically-computed sites fall back to the caller's value\" with ruling 6: computed call-pathway confidences become ruling-6 derivations; any remaining caller-valued site must be listed and justified (WI-famiv-gumof close condition)."  # 7b44
